---
layout: default
---
<div class="post deck-home">
  <header class="deck-hero" aria-label="Introduction">
    <div class="deck-copy">
      <div class="deck-eyebrow">Operations Research · Naval Postgraduate School</div>
      <h1 class="deck-brand">
        Will<br /><span>Kirschenman</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="deck-headline">Priority isn’t just order. It’s geometry.</p>
      <p class="deck-sub">
        Assistant Professor studying spatial optimization for layouts where fit is not enough —
        what must come off first, what stays together, and how the load balances.
        Combat load planning is the motivating case; the math travels.
        <a href="{{ '/research/' | relative_url }}">Research overview</a>
        ·
        <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>
      </p>
      <div class="deck-cta">
        <a class="deck-btn" href="#framework">Explore the framework</a>
        <a class="deck-btn ghost" href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}">Selected papers</a>
        <a class="deck-btn ghost" href="{{ '/writing/#press-and-coverage' | relative_url }}">Press</a>
      </div>
      {% if page.profile and page.profile.more_info %}
        <div class="more-info" style="font-size:0.75rem;color:var(--deck-mute);line-height:1.5;">
          {{ page.profile.more_info }}
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="deck-stage">
      <div class="deck-chrome">
        <span>Interactive deck · priority packing</span>
        <span><strong id="deck-fill">0%</strong> packed · click a crate</span>
      </div>
      <div class="deck-frame">
        <div class="deck-hint">Move mouse · click cargo</div>
        <canvas id="priority-deck" width="720" height="520" role="img" aria-label="Interactive priority packing diagram"></canvas>
        <div class="deck-ramp">← Access / ramp</div>
      </div>
      <div class="deck-legend">
        <span><i style="background:#1ec8c3"></i>Priority 1</span>
        <span><i style="background:#0891b2"></i>Priority 2</span>
        <span><i style="background:#5b8a9a"></i>Priority 3</span>
        <span><i style="background:#efe8dc"></i>Selected paper</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="deck-strip" aria-label="Highlights">
    <div class="deck-stat"><b>Omega · NRL</b><span>2026 refereed articles on prioritized packing</span></div>
    <div class="deck-stat"><b>Bonder</b><span>INFORMS Military &amp; Security Society scholarship</span></div>
    <div class="deck-stat"><b>3 thrusts</b><span>Bin → vessel → multi-vessel waves</span></div>
    <div class="deck-stat"><b>Julia · JuMP</b><span>Matheuristics, GA, GPU proxies</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="deck-section" id="framework">
    <div class="deck-sec-label">Dissertation framework</div>
    <h2>Three problems. One spatial idea.</h2>
    <p class="deck-prose">
      Classical packing asks whether everything fits. Useful plans also ask what has to come off first,
      what needs to stay together, and whether the center of gravity stays feasible.
      Click a thrust — the deck restacks around that objective.
    </p>
    <div class="deck-thrusts" id="deck-thrusts">
      <button type="button" class="deck-thrust active" data-mode="priority">
        <div class="num">01</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Prioritized 2-D orthogonal packing</h3>
          <p>A prioritization matrix pulls high-priority items toward the access point while related items cluster. Sliding-window matheuristic for scale.</p>
          <div class="links">
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/nav.70087">Naval Research Logistics</a>
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.31224/4647">Preprint</a>
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.8pk0p2p1z">Data &amp; code</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="deck-thrust" data-mode="balance">
        <div class="num">02</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Combat loading with load balancing</h3>
          <p>Hard center-of-gravity feasibility on a fixed deck with obstacles and separation rules. Matheuristic pipelines finish in minutes.</p>
          <div class="links">
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.omega.2026.103638">Omega</a>
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.31224/6041">Preprint</a>
            <a href="https://news.ncsu.edu/2026/08/cracking-the-packing-code-new-models-incorporate-item-priority-location-and-weight-distribution/">NC State News</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="deck-thrust" data-mode="fleet">
        <div class="num">03</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Multi-vessel selection &amp; wave scheduling</h3>
          <p>Bilevel assignment of groups to a heterogeneous fleet and landing waves. Genetic algorithm guided by a fast packing proxy.</p>
          <div class="links">
            <a href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}">Dissertation, 2026</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="deck-home-body">
    <article>
      <div class="clearfix deck-about-prose">{{ content }}</div>

      {% if page.news and site.announcements.enabled %}
        <h2><a href="{{ '/news/' | relative_url }}" style="color: inherit">News</a></h2>
        {% include news.liquid limit=true %}
      {% endif %}

      {% if page.selected_papers %}
        <h2><a href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}" style="color: inherit">Selected publications</a></h2>
        {% include selected_papers.liquid %}
      {% endif %}

      {% if page.social %}
        <div class="social">
          <div class="contact-icons">{% include social.liquid %}</div>
          <div class="contact-note">{{ site.contact_note }}</div>
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
